source_content_english:
The rabbit lost his carrot and went to the Black Cat Sheriff to report the crime. The Black Cat Sheriff finally targeted four animals, namely the fox, tiger, lion, and wolf, and the criminal was among them.
The fox said: I didn't steal the carrot;
The tiger said: The carrot was stolen by the wolf;
The lion said: The tiger stole the carrot;
The wolf said: I have never stolen a carrot.
It was later learned that only one of the four animals was telling the truth. Please ask: Who stole the carrots? ( )

Xiaoqiang, Xiaoming, and Xiaoyong participated in the mathematics competition. They came from schools A, B, and C respectively, and won the first, second, and third prizes respectively. A known:
($$1$$) Xiaoqiang is not a player from School A;
($$2$$) Xiao Ming is not a player from School B;
($$3$$) Players from school A are not the first prize;
($$4$$) The player from school B won the second prize;
($$5$$) Xiao Ming is not the third prize.
Based on the above situation, it can be judged that Xiaoyong is a contestant from the school and he won the first prize.
